# Server-local ignores.
#
# These duplicate the `server/`-prefixed rules in the monorepo's root
# .gitignore, and they exist because THIS DIRECTORY IS ALSO PUBLISHED ON ITS
# OWN. `git subtree split --prefix=server` makes server/ the repository root,
# and the root .gitignore does not come with it — so without this file the
# deploy repo would have no rule stopping `.env`, with real JWT keys, the
# password pepper and the database password, from being committed.
#
# Keep the two in step. A rule added to only one of them protects only one repo.

node_modules/
dist/
build/

# Secrets. .env.example is the template and IS tracked.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Local scratch and generated artefacts
.scratch/
*.log
coverage/
.DS_Store

# Prisma generates the client into node_modules; nothing to track here, but a
# local engine download can land in prisma/ on some platforms.
prisma/*.node

# tsx resolves its cache under $TMPDIR. On Windows that variable is sometimes
# unset, and the literal string "undefined" becomes the directory name — which
# is how a tree of compile-cache blobs once got committed here.
undefined/
